% This file contains celtic tunes that I play, or at least played at
% one time, on whistle and flute.  Even in the cases where I
% originally learned the tune from sheet music or other abc files, I
% have tried to give the music the way I play it.  They are given here
% in the approximate order I learned them.

% In some cases, the tunes as given here may be modified from their
% original form to be playable (by me) on a D whistle or flute, such
% as moving a some phrases up an octave or changing a few notes.  I
% have tried to give the original forms of tunes with only a comment
% about where I play it differently, but some have slipped past.

% Most of the guitar chordings were done by my mother Sue Shulman
% and are "by no means definitive."  As a matter of fact, nothing here
% is "definitive," if that word even has any meaning in the context of
% traditional music.  There will be errors in here, and different
% versions, missing parts, wrong notes, and all that.  C'est la vie.

% `Gan Ainm' means `no name'.

